# Redirects from Jake's previous site (retired when jakecaminero.com was
# pointed at Netlify). This is a hash-routed single-page app, so a target
# like "/#/project/<id>" is deliberate, not a typo — confirmed a server
# 301 with a "#" in its Location header is honored by the browser exactly
# like a normal link (the fragment is a client-side concern, the browser
# navigates to the full target including it; only the path portion ever
# reaches the server). www already 301s to the apex domain first and
# preserves the full path, so these match regardless of which one a link
# used.
#
# Anything not listed here — a typo, a link from somewhere we don't know
# about — falls through to the on-brand 404.html (Netlify serves that
# automatically for any unmatched path; no rule needed for it here).

